{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Baumeister1969-fourM",
  "Source": "P. W. Baumeister, \"Radiant power flow and absorptance in thin films,\" Appl. Opt. 8, 423-436 (1969). doi:10.1364/AO.8.000423 - Fig. 22 caption, p. 434 (Sec. VIII): air (HL)^7 H 1.845L M1 D1 M2 D2 M2 D1 M1 1.845L (HL)^9 quartz",
  "Notes": "Four-M (multiplex) UV bandpass filter at 2536 A: Al 150/250/250/150 A separated by cryolite spacers, matched and antireflected with n=1.55/1.36 quarter-wave stacks\nSpecification: Absorbing stack M1D1M2D2M2D1M1 with spacers varied for optimum Psi_max (D1 = QWOT at 4100 A, D2 = QWOT at 3900 A), then matched and antireflected.\nReported: p. 434-435: maximum transmittance 0.45 for the 150-250-250-150 A four-M filter (vs 0.003 for a single 800 A Al film in a one-M filter and 0.13 for an MDM with 400 A films). Fig. 22 (log T, 0.2-0.4 um; solid = nondispersive n = 0.2 - j2.8, dashed = Hunter dispersive): peak ~0.45 near 0.25 um, long-wave leak near 3000 A (solid ~0.1-0.2 from 0.28 to 0.4 um), ~1e-5 at 0.22 um. Check computed here (nondispersive): T = 0.4495, R = 0.001 at 253.6 nm; Psi_max of the absorbing stack 0.450 at Y_max ~1.92 + j4.74; T = 1.7e-5 at 220 nm, 0.16 at 300 nm.\nNotes: Normal incidence assumed (no angle given). The notation is read left to right from the incident medium (air) to the substrate (quartz, n = 1.47), so layer 1 is next to air. All dielectric layers are quarter-wave optical thickness (QWOT) at lambda0 = 2536 A = 253.6 nm with constant indices; the Al film is a physical thickness with the nondispersive n - jk = 0.20 - j2.80 at 2536 A (Macleod sign convention; k = +2.80 here). Per the Fig. 22 caption: H = QWOT at 2536 A, index 1.55; L, D1, D2 cryolite 1.36 with QWOT at 2536, 4100 and 3900 A (D1 = 410/253.6, D2 = 390/253.6 QWOT at 253.6 nm); M1 = Al 150 A, M2 = Al 250 A. Expanded: (HL)^7 (14), H, 1.845L, M1, D1, M2, D2, M2, D1, M1, 1.845L, (HL)^9 (18): 42 layers.\nLayers from Fig. 22 caption, p. 434 (Sec. VIII): air (HL)^7 H 1.845L M1 D1 M2 D2 M2 D1 M1 1.845L (HL)^9 quartz; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours T 0.450, R 0.001 at 253.6 nm; paper T 0.45 with R = 0 at 253.6 nm.",
